      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "A forex trader's annual profits have been *decreasing* continuously at a rate of $12\\%$ per year. Her profit this year is $\\$24900$. What was her profit $3$ years ago? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the continuously compounded growth equation $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The current amount is $P=24900$, the rate is $r=-0.12$ (negative for decay), and the elapsed time is $t=3$ years. The time unit matches the rate. Substitute and divide by the exponential factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n24900 &= P_0e^{(-0.12)(3)} \\\\\n24900 &= P_0e^{-0.36} \\\\\ne^{-0.36} &\\approx 0.69767633 \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{24900}{e^{-0.36}} \\\\\n&\\approx 35689.90242255 \\\\\n&\\approx 35690\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe earlier profit was $\\$35690$. Round only the final amount; keep full calculator precision in the exponential factor.",
